== Special education context of use?
Students with special educational needs in the areas of intellectual development, learning, and autism spectrum disorder (ASS) often face common challenges in the learning process. In addition to difficulties with fundamental prerequisites for learning, such as perseverance, memory, or motivation, they frequently experience challenges in learning how to learn. This may inlcude difficulties to reflect on their own learning, evaluate their learning processes, and transfer what they have learned to everyday situations. Problems in independent thinking, action planning, and problem-solving also play an important role, as these abilities enable learners to structure sequences of actions and cope with emerging problems independently (Kultusministerkonferenz, 2019, 2021).

Against the background of these challenges, the following areas of development and competence are particularly relevant:(quelle)
-  Action planning
-  Problem-solving
-  Recognition of relationships
-  Attention and memory
-  Motor skills and perception
-  Independence and self-regulation

Special educational provision therefore aims to support students in developing these competencies, enabling them to act with increasing independence and self-determination in both educational and everyday contexts and to participate more fully in society. Competence is reflected not only in the knowledge a person possesses, but particularly in their ability to make decisions, plan and carry out actions, evaluate their outcomes, and seek appropriate support when required (Kultusministerkonferenz, 2011, 2021).

=== Implications for Learning and Teaching
The heterogeneity of learner groups resulting from the three areas considered here, intellectual development, learning, and autism spectrum disorder (vergleich mit Table X), makes it difficult to select educational opportunities that are equally suitable for all learners. 

